WEBVTT

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.520
Supposedly the ancient Babylonians called it Nergal.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.340
In the face of new mysteries and the death of many people,

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:15.030
New mysteries and people's death.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:18.680
all we could do was run away.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:20.420
Kind of typical, isn't it?

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:56.560
The Forth Moon-seizing Battle

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.390
The Chulip is emitting graviton waves!

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:09.280
What?!

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.130
Emerging vessel is larger than Yamma class!

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:13.430
Let's see what you've got!

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.070
If push comes to shove, we'll ram the Gladiolus against you!

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.560
Graviton wave intensity continues to increase!

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.050
My God, can that be...

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.280
The Nadesico?!

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:42.470
The Luke Warm "Cold Equation"

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.460
Nadesico is returning to normal space.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.200
Currently calculating our position.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.520
Everyone, please wake up.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.710
Hey, yoohoo!

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:56.380
Please wake up!

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.740
Please wake up, everyone!

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:02.940
Return to your positions and observe emergency conditions.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:04.480
Captain!

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.870
Captain, Captain!

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.430
We have returned to normal space.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.170
Captain, what are you doing there?

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:22.750
No!

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:24.550
Captain?

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:27.130
Oh, let's see how it looks outside!

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:30.330
Yes, Ma'am. Projecting on observatory room screen.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:34.170
We are currently near the Moon, surrounded by Battas.

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:36.610
Configure Gravity Blast Cannon to wide spread!

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.220
Fire, then raise fields and pull back!

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.060
What the hell were you thinking?!

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:47.170
Fortunately, the blast missed. There were no deaths, but hear this!

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:52.010
If you fire again, we will respond with force to preserve our honor!

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:52.810
That is all!

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.420
I said it was a misunderstanding!

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.440
If misunderstandings could be solved easily, it would be simple.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:01.450
Ruri, what are the damages to the UEAF?

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:01.970
Damage Report

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:05.920
What blind luck. It looks like there are relatively few serious injuries.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.830
But who wouldn't get angry?

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.690
No point denying the fact that we nearly vaporized all of them.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:16.280
This after having been saved by a military man! We ought to be...

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:20.000
If you were on the bridge, you'd have grasped the situation better.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.550
Hey, Akito.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.570
Do you know what happened?

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.690
I want to know too! I want to know too!

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:29.720
Hey!

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.150
I want to know as well!

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.510
Megumi-chan!

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:35.320
Going to the observation room during an alert is inappropriate!

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:38.590
But with Inez-san there, I'm sure no mistakes were made.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:39.860
Mistakes?

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.220
Yeah, Inez-san!

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:46.410
It's about time that explanatory fetishist should come out.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:47.670
Inez-san!

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.620
Inez - Napping!

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:51.800
Hey, wait...

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.170
Well?

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.200
Like I said I don't...

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.920
Well? Well? Well?!

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.790
Enough of this!

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.390
Who cares what Tenkawa does on his own? So what?!

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.530
I'm going to trust Tenkawa!

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:09.100
What is it?

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:12.120
"I'm going to trust Tenkawa?"

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.120
Tenkawa...

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.150
Shut up, you two! We're supposed to be standing by.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:19.640
Tenkawa, Tenkawa, Tenkawa, Tenkawa!

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.530
The enemy's second attack wave is closing in.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:27.040
All units, spread out! Search and destroy!

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:28.190
Strategy?

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:29.420
Improvise!

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.250
Roger!

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:36.010
Maintain the field and stand by!

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.950
Remember to charge up the Gravity Blast Cannon.

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:39.750
Roger!

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:43.020
In any case, I wonder what we were doing there?

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.670
I recall being on the bridge...

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:48.940
Oh, if only I could be alone with Akito.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.670
Oh, Captain, I need to discuss something with you.

00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:53.270
It was nothing!

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:57.860
The main office would like to have a word with you.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:02.370
As I said, the main office requests to speak with you.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:03.370
I see...

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.220
Gotcha!

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.280
I don't believe it!

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.310
Only three out of ten?!

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:18.080
Looks like the Batta's fields have been reinforced as well.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.590
Weapons that evolve?

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:23.030
No problem.

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:25.930
We're one up on them when it comes to hand-to-hand combat!

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.640
What about Tenkawa? Tenkawa?!

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:30.850
Knock it off!

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:32.540
Tenkawa!

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:33.850
Tenkawa!

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.720
Where are you, Tenkawa?!

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:42.490
Respond, Tenkawa!

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:44.240
You idiot! What's going on over there?!

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.140
Damn it!

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:56.750
Hello, Akito-kun? Hello, hello, hello, hello?!

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.630
Tenkawa! Hold on, we'll be right there!

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.850
Tenkawa Aestivalis has been completely surrounded.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:02.600
What the hell is with me?

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:03.270
Akito-kun!

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.300
Calm down!

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:05.530
My hands won't move!

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:06.240
Akito-san...

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:07.940
Imagine all the Battas nude.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:09.150
Assist Tenkawa at once!

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:10.220
We're on our way!
Imagine all the Battas nude.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.140
You don't have to tell us!

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:22.010
What the hell's wrong with me?

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:24.120
I thought I finally had it licked.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.670
I wasn't afraid anymore.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:49.560
Tenkawa!

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:52.140
Step bask!

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:53.840
It's dangerous here.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.030
All units return to base immediately!

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:56.350
Hurry!

00:07:56.650 --> 00:07:58.130
Who the hell are you?!

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.490
Twenty percent of the enemy have been vaporized.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:05.400
You're kidding!

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:06.410
Detecting second volley.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:11.900
Amazing...

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:13.900
A multiple barreled Gravity Blast Cannon?

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:15.210
Then...

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:31.500
What the hell type of Frame is this?!

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.050
A new model already?

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:34.530
The head's different!

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.230
The generator is more compact!

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:38.980
And she's so smooth!

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:40.690
Keep it up, loser!

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:43.780
But I wonder, when did they build a new model?

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:49.070
We were told our Aesti-chan were the latest!
They cheated us!

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:50.400
That's a misunderstanding.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:55.900
Wow!

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:58.760
Eight months have passed since you disappeared from Mars,

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:02.200
and Earth has been steadily reinforcing its arsenal.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:03.670
Who the hell are you?!

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:08.460
I'm Akatsuki Nagare. The man from the Cosmos.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:11.000
Understood, Captain?

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:15.390
We expect that you will accept this proposal we have shown you.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.320
Or else the Nadesico will be caught in the crossfire

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:21.340
between the Space Forces under Gladiolus and the Jovians.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:24.150
Yes, but this is so sudden.

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:28.650
Well, to start, why don't we first sit down and have a nice meeting!

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:30.700
Sounds fine.

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:33.780
Then to start with, we'll have the Cosmos take in the Nadesico.

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:34.490
Cosmos?

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:37.580
Yes, Nadesico class battleship number two, Cosmos.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:55.440
Guidance beams, confirmed.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.550
Roger that!

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.890
Oh, this is so easy!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.110
It appears that going through the Chulip doesn't necessarily mean only teleportation.

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:17.410
At least eight months have passed since our fighting on Mars.

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:21.460
During this time, Nergal settled their differences with the UEAF,

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:24.240
built new battleships for them, and together they reclaimed the Moon.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:25.600
Based on my analysis, I would say that...

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:26.040
Well, yes, maybe at a later time!
Based on my analysis, I would say that...

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:27.300
Well, yes, maybe at a later time!

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:34.280
And so, Nergal has decided to coordinate its war efforts with that of the UEAF, leading us to... Captain?

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.940
Yes, and that means that the Nadesico

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:40.090
will be integrated into United Earth Navy Far Eastern Command.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:43.700
Are you telling us we're going to be soldiers from now on?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:46.990
No, that's not true. It means we temporarily cooperate with them.

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:47.940
And you are?

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.980
Akatsuki Nagare, a helping hand.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:56.870
Guess we're like pirates who've gathered around the flag of liberty.

00:10:57.330 --> 00:11:01.910
The rough ways of the military would be totally inappropriate for someone such as you.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:03.040
What about Mars?

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:08.160
Oh, yeah, Mars. Are we going to just give up on Mars?

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.270
Will we prevail if we go back again?

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:10.680
Even if...

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:13.840
"Even if we can't, we must try again and again,"

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:15.390
is a tactic that makes no sense at all,

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:18.100
and Nergal will not stand to suffer such losses.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.020
Strategically speaking,

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:22.940
it makes more sense to cooperate with the United Forces. But...

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:25.180
Are you telling us we have to be mercenaries?

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:29.640
If you don't like it, why don't you just take your pay and leave?

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:42.110
Today we have a new friend in our class. His name is Akara Ginji-kun.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:43.570
I'm Akara. It's nice to meet all of you.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:44.190
Wow! He's so cool!

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:44.940
Damn, I'm better looking than him!

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:45.630
Wow! He's so cool!

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:46.710
Damn, I'm better looking than him!

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:50.050
My God!

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:55.080
Just imagine! Earthlings have the same capacity for love as we do?!

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.660
This is an amazing discovery I have made!

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:02.810
Oh, you'll have to excuse me. The door was open.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:03.500
You!

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:05.930
Prepare yourself, Gekiganger!

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:07.720
Rowko'tsu! He's too eager for a kill!

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:09.360
Let's go, everyone!

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:11.420
It's time to launch Gekiganger!

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:13.410
What?! It can't be!

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:16.980
Ken and the gang are the pilots of the Gekiganger?!

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:18.520
Hurry, Ken! Your machine is ready to go!

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:20.310
You don't have to watch it if it makes you laugh.

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:20.840
I don't get it.
Hurry, Ken! Your machine is ready to go!

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:21.020
I don't get it.

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:22.200
Wow, Professor. You sure have everything covered!

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:24.100
You probably don't.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:24.280
Wow, Professor. You sure have everything covered!

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:26.530
If you like anime shows like that,

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:30.440
you should welcome the Nadesico joining the military.

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:32.610
What about yourself?!

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:33.940
Let's...

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:34.410
I'm just a man who enjoys fighting.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:35.350
Gekiga-in!
I'm just a man who enjoys fighting.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:36.280
I'm just a man who enjoys fighting.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:43.740
You're probably becoming aware that the lFS stimulates an aggressive, competitive nature within you.

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:47.850
I don't see why I have to be fighting in a war, just because a war is going on!

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:51.980
What's wrong with a life that has nothing to do with war?!

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:56.400
You're afraid, aren't you? Be honest.

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:59.040
All right! Gekigan Sword, assume Heaven's Rush Pose!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.070
Are you picking a fight?

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:05.840
Let's not fight. How about a good one-on-one game?

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:11.500
By the way, the gravity in this room is low, so be careful...

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:13.930
But I guess saying it now is a little too late.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:19.810
What's wrong? Act cool like they do in anime.

00:13:19.810 --> 00:13:20.720
Shut up!

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:24.160
Tenkawa-kun, create a counter force!

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:27.740
Damn it! Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.710
What? What? What?

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:32.640
There you are, Tenkawa-kun!

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:33.270
Shut up!

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:37.160
This is basketball! In a real fight...

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:41.500
Enemy approaching. Aestivalis pilots, prepare to intercept!

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.740
Come on, Akito, and you long-haired punk! Let's go!

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:48.280
Don't be lured away!

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:49.000
Roger!

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:51.200
Here's your long awaited moment in combat.

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:51.660
Shut up!

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:53.680
Assume battle formation!

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:54.590
Roger!

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:02.790
I like that. A very safe and reliable method of engagement.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.110
I'm not fighting this war because I want to!

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:07.050
Then why are you onboard the Nadesico?!

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.230
Damn it! So what if I'm onboard?

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.870
Damn you! Damn you! Damn you!

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:27.920
Hey, Akito! Let's get the Batta!

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:29.480
I don't think he can hear you.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:30.500
Akito!

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:37.320
Tenkawa Aestivalis, entering the shadow of the moon.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:37.750
Tenkawa Aestivalis, respond. Tenkawa Aestivalis, respond!

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:39.330
Graviton wave beam feed has been severed.

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:39.870
Tenkawa Aestivalis, respond. Tenkawa Aestivalis, respond!

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:40.950
He's marooned.

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:42.630
Marooned?

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.700
Will he be able to get back on his own?

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:46.580
Impossible.

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.970
With the graviton wave energy feed down,

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:52.400
he'll have to rely on power from the onboard backup battery.

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:53.510
That'll last less than five minutes of continuous flight.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:57.620
The best thing to do when you're lost is to stay in one place.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:59.460
I'll bet he'll do just that!

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:05.120
If we can get close to him, then his chances of returning increase.

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:08.280
But the Nadesico is currently undergoing repairs.

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:10.450
We'd be a sitting duck if we took off now.

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:14.490
Akatsuki-san, are there standard fighters on board the Cosmos?

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:16.440
Cosmos - Fuel-powered Catapult

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:20.280
You've got four hours of fuel. Come back if it gets hairy.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:20.880
Thank you.

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:23.540
I must say I'm taken aback at your willingness to go get him.

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:26.950
I thought you were a more intelligent person.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:29.520
Oh, I'm one of those newer types of captains.

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:33.910
But Megu-chan, you haven't received combat training.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:37.260
I had a pilot's license before I went to the training center.

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:39.980
And I have a reason as well.

00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:44.390
Okay, Jun-kun. I'll leave the rest to you!

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:46.490
Right! Because I'm your friend.

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:49.220
Catapult One, gate is open.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:50.720
Four...

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:51.550
Three...

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:52.240
Two...

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.040
One!

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:01.000
At best, another eight hours before the energy runs out.

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:03.700
Actually, the oxygen will run out before that.

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:07.750
Combat? Who?

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:12.320
Oh well, as if I could move at all anyway.

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:20.720
Imagine something like that actually becoming useful!

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:22.110
It's like Gekiganger.

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:28.030
Are you all right, Megu-chan?!

00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:29.620
I'm holding on!

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:36.540
Oh, thank God!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:39.870
You're my knight in shining armor, Akito!

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:41.500
Weren't you afraid?

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:42.800
Yes...

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:46.630
But when I realized that I had to help you two, I wasn't afraid.

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:48.990
I wonder why?

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:50.780
Was it for my sake?

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:51.670
What about me?

00:16:52.310 --> 00:16:55.060
Quit it! There's only thirty minutes of oxygen left!

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:56.520
Why?

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:58.090
That can't be helped.

00:16:58.090 --> 00:16:59.190
There are three of us.

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:00.190
Exactly!

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:01.560
So what are we going to do?

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:07.780
At this rate of acceleration,

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:11.580
we won't be in Nadesico's range for over two hours.

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:15.220
By the time two hours go by, we'll all be frozen stiff.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:15.870
All right!

00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:21.810
Now if we raise the emergency solar sail,

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.210
we'll be able to accelerate even faster, but...

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:24.950
Forty minutes.

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:26.290
What about the number at the bottom?

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:27.920
How can we get it to twenty minutes?

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:31.320
That's if there was only one person inside.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:32.470
For two, it'll take thirty minutes.

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:36.510
So if one of us got off, the others would get to the Nadesico sooner.

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:39.770
Then they could refuel and come back in a hurry.

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:42.250
Akito has to remain, because he's the pilot.

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:43.770
So...

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:46.880
I have to decide?

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:48.490
Then Yurika.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.410
Is it because I'm heavy?

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:53.720
That's right. You're a real burden on my shoulders.

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:54.910
That's why...

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.720
I'll get off!

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.010
No, Megu-chan!

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:00.700
I have to admit, I've been pigging out on meals that are really tasty.

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:02.830
That's not what this is about.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:04.320
Then what?

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:05.840
Well, it's...

00:18:07.490 --> 00:18:08.010
Gai...

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:09.570
That's it!

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:11.590
Yeah, I know!

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:17.910
No, Akito, I haven't gotten off yet!

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:19.530
It's all right. We'll go together.

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:23.060
Sacrificing one thing to save something else is the military way!

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:26.220
We'll work it out somehow, with our wits and guts!

00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:30.170
Our dreams call out for tomorrow...

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:33.190
System Down

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:36.320
Looks like we ran out of energy.

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:37.490
I'm sorry!

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:38.810
We may have strayed off course.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:41.110
Or else there wasn't enough acceleration.

00:18:41.110 --> 00:18:42.120
No, you didn't.

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:43.080
That's right!

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:47.240
Akito's my knight in shining armor, who saves me when I'm in trouble.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:49.440
This time it's my turn!

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:53.220
So for you, Akito is just someone you look up to?

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:56.160
I love Akito-san!

00:18:57.800 --> 00:18:59.100
I suspected as much.

00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:02.690
But Akito is someone special to me too!

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:06.220
I'm not sure if it's the same kind as yours, Megumi-san

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:08.610
Tell me your feelings, Akito-san!

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:10.480
Why were you in the observation room?

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:13.560
Akito, you kissed Megu-chan, didn't you?

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:14.240
What was...

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:16.090
I want to know too!

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:16.860
So do I!

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:18.040
I wouldn't mind knowing!

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:19.530
I'm not interested, but...

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:22.520
If communications have been restored...

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:28.830
You're the last person I'd imagine willing to take this kind of risk.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:31.940
There's no fun without him around.

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:35.340
Akatsuki-san, I'm going to stay on the Nadesico!

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:37.090
So you've finally come around.

00:19:37.090 --> 00:19:39.870
That's right, that flame that you feel burning...

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:41.350
I have something I want to protect!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.390
It's Gai!

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:46.620
He always wanted to fight for the sake of the Earth.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.360
But he wasn't eager to fight a war.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:50.060
Cool! So that's going to be his take on all this!

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:52.550
I don't know how to put this, but I want to find something like that.

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:52.780
Cool! So that's going to be his take on all this!

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:55.410
Yeah, sounds like something he'd say.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.750
Oh no, it's not going to end just like that!

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:11.760
He's the new admiral assigned to our ship.

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:13.580
I'm looking forward to this!

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:18.650
I'm Erina Kinjo Won. I've been assigned as your new co-helmswoman.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:20.100
Well, there you have it.

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:22.600
But why is the chairman's secretary coming aboard?

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:26.110
I didn't expect you to be on board.

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:27.210
Will I be in your way?

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:28.050
Well...

00:20:28.050 --> 00:20:29.110
So, what's up?

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:33.720
This is footage of Tenkawa Akito at the moment of the boson jump.

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:34.150
Watch.

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:35.680
Well, well!

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:38.780
I like him.

00:21:44.380 --> 00:21:46.020
Destination: the Arctic Ocean!

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:47.970
Having been given this mysterious command,

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:50.310
what awaits the Nadesico on the frozen surface of the open sea?

00:21:50.310 --> 00:21:53.170
Will Akito make it back alive?

00:21:53.170 --> 00:21:57.460
At the same time, another affair is taking up Akito's attention.

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:59.540
Next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:01.610
"The Miracle Operation of The Kiss?!"

00:22:01.610 --> 00:22:02.990
Let's watch it, everyone!

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:05.710
You'll be able to see Megumi-oneesan in sailor uniform.
